- Use SQLite database with k.DB.sqlite
- Tables automatically have _id primary key
- Create records with k.DB.sqlite.tableName.append({})
- Use named parameters for SQL queries: k.DB.sqlite.query(sql, { key1: value1 })
- Use @key as parameter placeholders in SQL
- For transactions, use k.DB.sqlite.transaction(() => {})
- Throw errors inside transactions to abort them
- Transaction blocks don't return values
- Operations involving multiple tables must use transactions